## Rounded

If we want rounded borders, we can add `border-radius: .5em`:

![Border Radius](assets/1816674/737172fa.png)

— But that doesn't seem to work for the image … we need to set:

```css
.card {
  border-radius: .5em;
  & img {
    border-start-start-radius: inherit;
    border-start-end-radius: inherit;
  }
}
```

— **OR** we can use `clip-path`:

```css
.card {
  clip-path: inset(0 round .5em);
}
```

![Border Radius and clippath](assets/1816674/c184bccf.png)


The result is the same, but `clip-path` will also cut off box-shadows and borders, should you need them.

And that concludes this tutorial! As you can see, a card-component can be _super simple_, with a **lot** of flexibility through the power of CSS grids.

